  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2006-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Note that \\[ CDCD = 101 \\cdot CD. \\] This forces \\(ABA = 101.\\) Then \\(A = 1,\\) \\(B = 0,\\) and \\(A + B = 1.\\)\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(CDCD\\) as \\(100\\cdot CD+CD\\).",
        "Since \\(CD\\) is nonzero, divide the equation by the two-digit number \\(CD\\)."
